51151202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NtGNi","user":{"login":"SbhnP","id":114316833,"node_id":"U_kgDOBtBWIQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114316833?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP","html_url":"https://github.com/SbhnP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SbhnP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-27T12:57:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T13:03:32Z","body":"@AThousandShips \nIt will work if the CustomNodeScene  class is [Tool]:\n```cs\nusing Godot;\nusing System;\n\n[Tool]\npublic partial class CustomNodeScene : Node2D\n{\n    public void CustomPrint(string text)\n    {\n        GD.Print(text);\n    }\n}\n\n```\nThen it can be instantiated like this:\n`  _customNodeScene = packedScene.Instantiate<CustomNodeScene>(); `\n```cs\n    CustomNodeScene _customNodeScene;\n\n    public override void _Ready()\n    {\t\t\n        var packedScene = GD.Load<PackedScene>(\"res://src/CustomNode/custom_node.tscn\");\n        _customNodeScene = packedScene.Instantiate<CustomNodeScene>();\n        AddChild(_customNodeScene);\n        _customNodeScene.Owner=GetTree().EditedSceneRoot;\n    }\n```\nThis solves the problem. \nBut I'm not sure if this is the right way to do it in every scenario (using [Tool] on anything which is instantiated and used in editor mode)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.gith